From: =?UTF-8?q?Eduardo=20Garc=C3=ADa-M=C3=A1dico=20Portabella?=
 <woodyst@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 17 Jul 2026 15:33:40 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 051/106] media: qcom: camss: keep sm7150's CSIPHY RX clock at
 the vendor rate

camcc_csiphy0_clk is a branch of camcc_cphy_rx_clk_src and carries
CLK_SET_RATE_PARENT, so whatever rate camss asks of it lands on the RCG
that feeds the CSIPHY's RX path - and the same RCG feeds every other
CSIPHY and the IFEs.

The rate list here starts at 300000000, and the rate picker takes the
first entry above the link frequency over four, so a 953.6MHz link picks
300MHz. The vendor device tree asks for 384MHz at its lowest performance
level and 400MHz above that, and never sets csiphy0_clk itself:

	clock-names = "cphy_rx_clk_src", "csiphy0_clk", ...
	clock-rates = <384000000 0 300000000 0>, <400000000 0 300000000 0>, ...

Drop the 300MHz entry so the shared RCG lands on 384MHz, as measured in
clk_summary while streaming on a POCO X3 NFC.

Note that cphy_rx_src's own list is dead data: csiphy_set_clock_rates()
only sets clocks whose name matches csiphy%d_timer or csiphy%d, so the
rate has to be asked for through the branch.
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss.c
index d18b0aefc..b6aadd1a8 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss.c
@@ -1713,8 +1713,8 @@ static const struct camss_subdev_resources csiphy_res_7150[] = {
 		},
 		.clock = { "cphy_rx_src", "csiphy0", "csiphy0_timer_src", "csiphy0_timer" },
 		.clock_rate = { { 0 },
-				{ 300000000, 384000000, 400000000 },
-				{ 0 },	
+				{ 384000000, 400000000 },
+				{ 0 },
 				{ 300000000 } },
 		.reg = { "csiphy0" },
 		.interrupt = { "csiphy0" },
